1
00:00:00,354 --> 00:00:07,081
In this video, we'll set up Job Explorer from scratch, and go all the way to your first list of AI-scored jobs.

2
00:00:08,348 --> 00:00:12,377
The first time you open Job Explorer, a short setup walks you through it.

3
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:15,558
It starts by explaining how your information is handled.

4
00:00:16,423 --> 00:00:20,703
Your profile, resumes, and applications stay on your computer, encrypted.

5
00:00:20,886 --> 00:00:23,875
There's no account, and nothing is sent to the app's maker.

6
00:00:24,734 --> 00:00:29,798
When the AI scores a job, only what it needs is sent, like the posting and your skills.

7
00:00:29,977 --> 00:00:33,001
Your name and contact details are removed first.

8
00:00:33,188 --> 00:00:36,156
With local AI, nothing leaves your computer at all.

9
00:00:37,017 --> 00:00:39,262
And Job Explorer never applies for you.

10
00:00:39,443 --> 00:00:43,408
You apply on the employer's own site, then mark the job as applied.

11
00:00:44,274 --> 00:00:46,333
You can also choose the app's language here.

12
00:00:46,512 --> 00:00:47,642
Let's get started.

13
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,134
Next, choose your AI.

14
00:00:53,326 --> 00:00:58,089
Job Explorer uses it to read each job posting, and score how well it fits you.

15
00:00:58,945 --> 00:01:03,387
Local AI runs right on your computer, with a free program called Ollama.

16
00:01:03,573 --> 00:01:06,759
It's the most private option, and it costs nothing to use.

17
00:01:07,623 --> 00:01:13,091
Cloud AI uses Claude, ChatGPT, or Gemini, with your own API key.

18
00:01:13,274 --> 00:01:16,931
It's fast and capable, and the provider bills you for what you use.

19
00:01:17,799 --> 00:01:19,044
We'll use local AI.

20
00:01:19,912 --> 00:01:22,198
Job Explorer checks your computer first.

21
00:01:22,387 --> 00:01:27,574
Here it found a graphics card with eight gigabytes of memory, and recommends a model that suits it.

22
00:01:28,439 --> 00:01:32,792
If you don't have Ollama yet, install it from the Ollama website, then start it.

23
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:35,737
On this computer, it's already installed and running.

24
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:38,232
Then pick a model to download.

25
00:01:38,414 --> 00:01:40,485
The recommended one is marked for you.

26
00:01:40,670 --> 00:01:44,268
Bigger models give better results, but need a bigger graphics card.

27
00:01:45,130 --> 00:01:50,251
Click use, and Job Explorer runs a quick test to make sure the model works on your computer.

28
00:01:55,788 --> 00:01:56,942
Now add your resume.

29
00:01:57,130 --> 00:01:59,948
Job Explorer reads Word and PDF files.

30
00:02:00,805 --> 00:02:03,081
Click import resume, and choose your file.

31
00:02:03,941 --> 00:02:11,399
It reads the resume, and turns it into suggestions for your profile, like your summary, work history, education, and skills.

32
00:02:12,264 --> 00:02:14,311
Nothing is used until you approve it.

33
00:02:14,499 --> 00:02:15,817
We'll do that in a moment.

34
00:02:16,685 --> 00:02:17,684
That's setup done.

35
00:02:17,869 --> 00:02:18,649
Click finish.

36
00:02:19,506 --> 00:02:22,016
Job Explorer then opens its built-in guide.

37
00:02:22,203 --> 00:02:26,357
It covers every feature, and you can come back to it any time from the sidebar.

38
00:02:29,761 --> 00:02:30,884
Open your Profile.

39
00:02:31,070 --> 00:02:34,367
Everything taken from the resume is waiting for your review.

40
00:02:35,233 --> 00:02:39,402
Your contact details are only used on resumes and letters you create.

41
00:02:39,585 --> 00:02:41,583
They're never sent to an AI provider.

42
00:02:42,445 --> 00:02:45,368
Check each item, and fix anything that's wrong with edit.

43
00:02:45,548 --> 00:02:46,499
Then approve it.

44
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:50,994
Only approved information is used to score jobs and build resumes.

45
00:02:51,859 --> 00:02:54,599
Everything here looks right, so we'll approve each item.

46
00:02:54,779 --> 00:03:00,673
As you approve them, they move from needs review to approved, until the whole profile is ready to use.

47
00:03:01,532 --> 00:03:05,050
Imported resumes start as drafts, so approve the resume too.

48
00:03:05,229 --> 00:03:07,596
Open Resumes, and click approve resume.

49
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:13,770
Next, tell Job Explorer what you're looking for.

50
00:03:13,950 --> 00:03:16,333
Open Searches, and create your first search.

51
00:03:17,198 --> 00:03:20,083
Give it a name, then add the job titles you want.

52
00:03:20,270 --> 00:03:21,868
Press enter after each one.

53
00:03:23,626 --> 00:03:26,118
Describe the job you want in your own words.

54
00:03:26,297 --> 00:03:29,516
The AI uses this to judge how well each job fits.

55
00:03:30,370 --> 00:03:32,580
Add the skills you want the job to center on.

56
00:03:32,771 --> 00:03:36,964
You can also list skills you have, but don't want as the main part of the job.

57
00:03:37,837 --> 00:03:39,187
Then choose where you'll work.

58
00:03:39,367 --> 00:03:45,784
Onsite and hybrid jobs can be limited to cities near you, and remote jobs to the countries you can work in.

59
00:03:46,639 --> 00:03:52,863
Below that are more filters, like a minimum salary, seniority, and how recent a posting must be.

60
00:03:53,047 --> 00:03:55,048
The defaults are a good place to start.

61
00:03:55,907 --> 00:03:58,001
When you're happy with it, click save search.

62
00:04:01,434 --> 00:04:04,007
Now choose where Job Explorer looks for jobs.

63
00:04:04,192 --> 00:04:05,546
Open Job Sources.

64
00:04:06,415 --> 00:04:08,586
The main source is companies you watch.

65
00:04:08,770 --> 00:04:15,229
Paste a company's careers page from Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, or SmartRecruiters, then click add company.

66
00:04:16,084 --> 00:04:17,283
We'll add a couple more.

67
00:04:17,464 --> 00:04:24,033
Every time a search runs, it checks every company on your list, and keeps only the jobs that pass your filters.

68
00:04:24,213 --> 00:04:26,512
You can watch as many companies as you like.

69
00:04:27,377 --> 00:04:33,693
If you use a cloud AI key, find companies can search the web for employers that hire for your job title.

70
00:04:34,554 --> 00:04:39,917
Below, you can add USAJOBS for federal jobs in the United States, with a free key.

71
00:04:40,103 --> 00:04:44,008
And you can block companies you never want to see, like your current employer.

72
00:04:47,416 --> 00:04:50,033
Back on Searches, open the search you just made.

73
00:04:50,891 --> 00:04:54,289
Preview shows what your filters keep, without using any AI.

74
00:04:54,479 --> 00:04:56,199
It's a quick way to check your settings.

75
00:04:57,990 --> 00:05:03,402
It shows how many postings it found, how many passed your filters, and why the rest were left out.

76
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:06,375
When it looks right, click run search now.

77
00:05:06,567 --> 00:05:10,589
The AI reads each job that passed, and scores it against your profile.

78
00:05:11,456 --> 00:05:15,282
With local AI, this takes a few minutes, depending on your computer.

79
00:05:15,464 --> 00:05:17,464
You can keep using the app while it runs.

80
00:05:20,438 --> 00:05:20,939
Done.

81
00:05:21,123 --> 00:05:23,291
The new jobs are waiting in your Review List.

82
00:05:27,723 --> 00:05:29,097
Here are your first results.

83
00:05:29,282 --> 00:05:34,685
Each job gets a score from zero to a hundred, and the best fits are marked as strong matches.

84
00:05:35,546 --> 00:05:39,457
Each one has a short reason, and a heads up when something needs a closer look.

85
00:05:40,316 --> 00:05:43,918
Click details to see exactly why it fits, and where the gaps are.

86
00:05:47,468 --> 00:05:50,785
Open posting takes you to the job on the employer's site.

87
00:05:50,965 --> 00:05:52,047
That's where you apply.

88
00:05:52,905 --> 00:05:56,196
Then come back and mark it applied, and it moves to your Tracker.

89
00:05:56,382 --> 00:05:58,527
Or decline it, or save it for later.

90
00:05:59,390 --> 00:06:01,166
Jobs with low scores are hidden.

91
00:06:01,345 --> 00:06:04,061
Tick show low scores to see everything the search found.

92
00:06:06,785 --> 00:06:07,493
That's it.

93
00:06:07,679 --> 00:06:10,240
You've gone from setup to your first list of jobs.

94
00:06:10,422 --> 00:06:13,894
Next, try Searcher Mode, to run your searches automatically.

95
00:06:14,076 --> 00:06:15,190
Thanks for watching.
